I just want to chime in and say that I really wish Nethack had larger
levels, or perhaps made better use of the space in the current ones. 
More frequent items perhaps, but this is the same problem with adding
more levels to the game: subtlely adjusting item frequencies would fix
that.  Changing the arbitrary size of a dungeon level would only
really break other arbitrary factors.

And I don't think it'd break monster difficulty at all: more rooms
means more starting monsters, and more moves to cross the dungeon
means more frequently-appearing wandering monsters.

It would affect the game in a number of small ways (it'd be harder to
track down thieving nymphs and leps), but nothing that would break the
game from a balance standpoint.

